  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_004: image_only, singleprofile, ViT-L → 22.7% acc), leaving almost no information about whether the RNA modality contributes any signal for this task. Uncertainty: The most fundamental open question is whether RNA expression provides useful classification signal at all, independent of image. Question tested: config_009 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200, no aggregation/fusion) establishes a clean RNA-only baseline using a well-validated single-cell embedding (scVI), with the same singleprofile setting as the image baseline to keep the comparison fair. Why best next step: With only one data point, the highest-value experiment is one that isolates a single modality's contribution. If RNA-only performs comparably to image-only, both modalities carry signal and multimodal fusion is worth pursuing; if it is much worse, image dominates and we should focus budget on image-side improvements. This simple, low-confound experiment reduces the largest source of uncertainty before committing budget to more complex multimodal configurations where multiple variables (RNA encoder, aggregation, fusion) would be entangled."
}

